<workout_file>
    <author>Coach Library</author>
    <name>Ramp Test</name>
    <description>PICK THIS WHEN: Same purpose as the 20-min test but shorter; use the same test type each time so results are comparable.
DAY TYPE: Special.

Tests &amp; Openers. Ramp Test.

Structure: 5 min warm-up, 1 min @ 52%, 1 min @ 58%, 1 min @ 64%, 1 min @ 70%, 1 min @ 76%, 1 min @ 82%, 1 min @ 88%, 1 min @ 94%, 1 min @ 100%, 1 min @ 106%, 1 min @ 112%, 1 min @ 118%, 1 min @ 124%, 1 min @ 130%, 1 min @ 136%, 1 min @ 142%, 1 min @ 148%, 1 min @ 154%, 1 min @ 160%, 1 min @ 166%, 1 min @ 172%, 1 min @ 178%, 10 min cool-down.

Coach notes: Ramp test (TrainerRoad-style protocol): 1-minute steps starting at 46% FTP, +6% per step. Ride until failure, then your new FTP is 75% of the best 1-minute power. Shorter and less painful than the 20-min test, slightly less accurate for riders with a strong sprint.

Duration: 37 min. Estimated TSS: 58 (tests depend on your effort).</description>
    <sportType>bike</sportType>
    <tags>
        <tag name="Test"/>
    </tags>
    <workout>
        <Warmup Duration="300" PowerLow="0.40" PowerHigh="0.46">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="Ramp test. 1-minute steps, +6% each. Ride until you cannot hold the step - do not pace."/>
            <textevent timeoffset="180" message="2 minutes to the main set. Lift the effort slightly."/>
        </Warmup>
        <SteadyState Duration="60" Power="0.52">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="Step 1: 52%."/>
        </SteadyState>
        <SteadyState Duration="60" Power="0.58">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="Step 2: 58%."/>
        </SteadyState>
